A repository validator treats every `cs.CG` paper as non-discrete unless a paper citation licenses the discrete formulation. Here that guard is broader than the paper—the paper’s native object really is a DAG—but the fixed-spine specialization still has an explicit license in Section 2 and Theorem 9. I’m recording that as a paper-licensed specialization (not a convenience reduction) so the schema remains transparent and the validator does not misclassify it.
